{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261024T014655Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "273647658eb97da96905e8e7", "title": "Scaling NVIDIA TensorRT Performance Optimization Beyond a Single Build Route with the Global Performance Tuner, Part 2", "url": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/scaling-nvidia-tensorrt-performance-optimization-beyond-a-single-build-route-with-the-global-performance-tuner-part-2/", "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog", "published": "2026-10-23T17:27:52+00:00", "is_ai": 0.96, "worthiness": 0.79, "worthiness_confidence": 0.86, "final_score": 0.79, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 15063, "delivered": true, "summary": "NVIDIA released the Global Performance Tuner in TensorRT 11.1, an automatic tuning system that explores multiple compiler \"build routes\" (combinations of knob settings) to optimize model performance while maintaining accuracy constraints. The feature matters because different models benefit from different scheduling strategies—tuning delivered 1.14x to 1.63x speedups across tested workloads by systematically evaluating alternatives. The key insight is treating accuracy as an explicit constraint that filters candidates, then selecting the fastest among acceptable options, solving the performance-accuracy tradeoff through measurement rather than heuristics. Developers can use provided APIs or the trtexec implementation with strategies like fast search (vary one knob), mixed search (explore promising combinations), or full search for small knob sets.", "jev_ms": 142.9, "jev_input_tokens": 3518, "jev_cost": 0.000147756, "llm_ms": 3422.9, "llm_cost": 0.004152, "errors": []}
{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261024T014655Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "a57112b0e367d105fef1ebb3", "title": "Scaling NVIDIA TensorRT Performance Optimization Beyond a Single Build Route with the Global Performance Tuner, Part 1", "url": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/scaling-nvidia-tensorrt-performance-optimization-beyond-a-single-build-route-with-the-global-performance-tuner-part-1/", "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog", "published": "2026-10-23T17:27:35+00:00", "is_ai": 0.98, "worthiness": 0.8125, "worthiness_confidence": 0.76, "final_score": 0.8125, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 16706, "delivered": true, "summary": "NVIDIA released Global Performance Tuner in TensorRT 11.1, an automatic performance tuning feature addressing the scaling problem of model-specific heuristics in deep learning compilation. The tool solves the challenge that different models benefit from different scheduling decisions around graph transformations, fusion, kernel selection, and quantization, making universal heuristics increasingly unmaintainable. Rather than encoding every optimization into one strategy, the tuner generates multiple customizable build routes, validates them against accuracy constraints, and selects the fastest feasible solution. Key takeaway: performance optimization should be accuracy-aware and model-dependent, using end-to-end measurement rather than relying on individual kernel profiling or accumulated heuristics.", "jev_ms": 166.2, "jev_input_tokens": 3871, "jev_cost": 0.000162582, "llm_ms": 3017.9, "llm_cost": 0.004517, "errors": []}
